    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14769" root="رثم" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَثِيمٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَرْثُومٌ</span>, in two places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَصًى رَثِيمٌ</span>
<i>Pebbles broken in pieces;</i> as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَثْمٌ</span></b> : (T:) or
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَثيمُ الحَصَى</span> means <i>what are crushed, of the
pebbles, by the feet of camels.</i> (TA.)

